>> title: Nanaimo Bars
>> category: Bars & Brownies
>> tags: chocolate, coconut, custard, no-bake, dessert
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: nanaimo squares
>> servings: 9
>> time: 2 hr
>> step.3: stir in, then press into the pan

Line an #8x8-in pan{} with parchment, leaving an overhang on two sides.

Cook @unsalted butter{1/2%cup}(115 g), @granulated sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @unsweetened cocoa powder{1/4%cup}(25 g), @egg{1%large}(50 g) in a #double boiler{} until thickened.

Stir @graham cracker crumbs{1 3/4%cup}(175 g), @shredded sweetened coconut{1%cup}(85 g), @finely chopped almonds{1/2%cup}(60 g) into @&(~1)cocoa custard{}, then press firmly into the pan.

Beat @unsalted butter{1/4%cup}(60 g), @custard powder{2%Tbs}(16 g; Bird's), @heavy cream{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @powdered sugar{2%cup}(240 g) until fluffy.

Spread @&(~1)custard buttercream{} over @&(~2)crumb base{} and chill ~{30%min}.

Melt @semisweet chocolate{4%oz}(115 g), @unsalted butter{1%Tbs}(14 g).

Pour @&(~1)chocolate glaze{} over @&(~2)chilled filling{}, then chill until just set.
